{"absent":["Locking, concurrency, preemption and interrupt-safety rules for trace fast paths are not shown.","Ring-buffer reservation, allocation, commit, overwrite and overflow handling are not shown.","Tracepoint enable, disable, filter evaluation and callback registration lifecycle are not shown.","Definitions of referenced helpers and constants such as sequence printers, null-string placeholder, formatted-string limits, nanoseconds-per-second, bits-per-word and cpu-mask bit count beyond their use are not shown.","Error handling for allocation failure, truncation beyond locator width, or malformed format strings is not shown."],"dossier":"D13","findings":[{"kind":"export","sids":["include/trace/stages/stage1_struct_define.h::TP_STRUCT__entry","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::TP_printk","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::TP_fast_assign","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__perf_count","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__perf_task"],"text":"Event authors use three passthrough wrappers: one carries the declared entry fields, one carries a print format plus arguments with trailing newline behavior, and one carries the fast-assignment body. Two perf helpers pass a counter expression and a task expression through unchanged."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/trace/stages/stage1_struct_define.h::__bitmask","include/trace/stages/stage1_struct_define.h::__cpumask","include/trace/stages/stage1_struct_define.h::__sockaddr","include/trace/stages/stage1_struct_define.h::__rel_dynamic_array","include/trace/stages/stage1_struct_define.h::__rel_string","include/trace/stages/stage1_struct_define.h::__rel_string_len","include/trace/stages/stage1_struct_define.h::__rel_bitmask","include/trace/stages/stage1_struct_define.h::__rel_cpumask","include/trace/stages/stage1_struct_define.h::__rel_sockaddr"],"text":"Entry-definition stage models variable payload uniformly: bit and cpu masks become character dynamics with open length, socket addresses become byte dynamics with caller length, and every relative string, mask or address is represented in the entry by one 32-bit locator word."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__field","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__field_ext","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__field_struct","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__field_struct_ext","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__array","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__dynamic_array","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__string","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__string_len","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__vstring","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__bitmask","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__cpumask","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__sockaddr","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__rel_dynamic_array","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__rel_string","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__rel_string_len","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__rel_bitmask","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__rel_cpumask","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__rel_sockaddr"],"text":"Offset-companion stage builds a parallel structure where fixed fields, extended fields, struct fields and static arrays contribute nothing, while each absolute or relative dynamic contributes a 32-bit slot plus a saved source pointer. Strings map to character dynamics, masks to unsigned-long dynamics, socket addresses keep byte element type."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__get_dynamic_array","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__get_dynamic_array_len","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__get_str","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__get_sockaddr","include/trace/stages/stage5_get_offsets.h::__dynamic_array","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__dynamic_array"],"text":"Absolute dynamic locators pack byte offset in the low 16 bits and byte length in the high 16 bits of one 32-bit word. Readers mask the low half for offset from the entry base and shift the high half for length; string helpers view the payload as characters and socket helpers as socket address structures."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__get_rel_dynamic_array","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__get_rel_dynamic_array_len","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__get_rel_str","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__get_rel_sockaddr","include/trace/stages/stage5_get_offsets.h::__rel_dynamic_array","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__rel_dynamic_array"],"text":"Relative dynamic locators use the same low-offset and high-length 16-bit split, but the offset is measured from the end of the locator field itself: readers add the locator position plus its size plus the stored offset. Length decoding mirrors the absolute case, with parallel string and socket views."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/trace/stages/stage4_event_fields.h::ALIGN_STRUCTFIELD","include/trace/stages/stage4_event_fields.h::__field_ext","include/trace/stages/stage4_event_fields.h::__field_struct_ext","include/trace/stages/stage4_event_fields.h::__field","include/trace/stages/stage4_event_fields.h::__field_struct","include/trace/stages/stage4_event_fields.h::__array","include/trace/stages/stage4_event_fields.h::__dynamic_array","include/trace/stages/stage4_event_fields.h::__string","include/trace/stages/stage4_event_fields.h::__string_len","include/trace/stages/stage4_event_fields.h::__vstring","include/trace/stages/stage4_event_fields.h::__bitmask","include/trace/stages/stage4_event_fields.h::__cpumask","include/trace/stages/stage4_event_fields.h::__sockaddr","include/trace/stages/stage4_event_fields.h::__rel_dynamic_array","include/trace/stages/stage4_event_fields.h::__rel_string","include/trace/stages/stage4_event_fields.h::__rel_string_len","include/trace/stages/stage4_event_fields.h::__rel_bitmask","include/trace/stages/stage4_event_fields.h::__rel_cpumask","include/trace/stages/stage4_event_fields.h::__rel_sockaddr"],"text":"Field-metadata stage emits one descriptor per declaration with textual type and name, byte size, alignment derived from wrapping the type in a host struct, signedness, filter class and, for static arrays, element count. Absolute dynamics use a data-loc type label and relative dynamics a rel-loc label, each four bytes in size and alignment; cpu-mask forms use dedicated cpumask type labels and report unsigned."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/trace/stages/stage5_get_offsets.h::__STAGE5_STRING_SRC_H","include/trace/stages/stage5_get_offsets.h::__string_src","include/trace/stages/stage5_get_offsets.h::__string","include/trace/stages/stage5_get_offsets.h::__string_len","include/trace/stages/stage5_get_offsets.h::__vstring","include/trace/stages/stage5_get_offsets.h::__rel_string","include/trace/stages/stage5_get_offsets.h::__rel_string_len","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__assign_str","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__assign_rel_str"],"text":"String sizing always reserves termination: plain strings measure the null-safe source plus one, bounded strings add one to the caller bound, formatted strings use a helper measuring the formatted output. A null source is replaced by a shared null placeholder when measuring and when copying; assignment copies length-minus-one bytes then writes termination. Relative strings follow the same rules."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/trace/stages/stage5_get_offsets.h::__bitmask_size_in_bytes_raw","include/trace/stages/stage5_get_offsets.h::__bitmask_size_in_longs","include/trace/stages/stage5_get_offsets.h::__bitmask_size_in_bytes","include/trace/stages/stage5_get_offsets.h::__bitmask","include/trace/stages/stage5_get_offsets.h::__cpumask","include/trace/stages/stage5_get_offsets.h::__rel_bitmask","include/trace/stages/stage5_get_offsets.h::__rel_cpumask","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__assign_bitmask","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__assign_cpumask","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__assign_rel_bitmask","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__assign_rel_cpumask"],"text":"Bitmask storage rounds a bit count up to whole bytes, then up to whole machine words, then back to bytes. Dynamic sizing counts words while copy size counts bytes; cpu-mask variants implicitly use the global cpu-mask bit count. Absolute and relative mask families share the sizing functions."},{"kind":"entry_point","sids":["include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__entry","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__get_bitmask","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__get_cpumask","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__get_rel_bitmask","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__get_rel_cpumask","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__get_sockaddr","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__get_rel_sockaddr","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__get_buf","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__event_in_hardirq","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__event_in_softirq","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__event_in_irq"],"text":"Output stage exposes accessors for the entry record, strings, masks and socket addresses plus interrupt-context tests and a sequence-buffer acquirer. Mask getters fetch pointer and length then delegate to a bitmask sequence printer, with cpu-mask aliases reusing mask logic; absolute and relative families stay distinct."},{"kind":"entry_point","sids":["include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__print_flags","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__print_symbolic","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__print_hex","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__print_hex_str","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__print_array","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__print_dynamic_array","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__print_hex_dump","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__print_ns_to_secs","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__print_ns_without_secs"],"text":"Formatting helpers cover flag sets and symbolic values, raw and string hex output, fixed arrays, dynamic arrays, generic hex dumps and time splitting. Flag and symbolic forms build a static table and delegate to a sequence printer; array printing constrains element width to one, two, four or eight bytes; dynamic arrays derive pointer and element count from the stored byte length."},{"kind":"entry_point","sids":["include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__entry","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__field","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__field_struct","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__array","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__string","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__string_len","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__vstring","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__assign_str","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__assign_vstr","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__bitmask","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__get_bitmask","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__assign_bitmask","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__cpumask","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__get_cpumask","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__assign_cpumask","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__sockaddr","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__get_sockaddr","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__assign_sockaddr","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__rel_string","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__rel_string_len","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__assign_rel_str","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__rel_bitmask","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__get_rel_bitmask","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__assign_rel_bitmask","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__rel_cpumask","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__get_rel_cpumask","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__assign_rel_cpumask","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__rel_sockaddr","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__get_rel_sockaddr","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__assign_rel_sockaddr"],"text":"Callback stage propagates computed offsets into entry locator words and copies payloads: fixed fields and static arrays are ignored, strings copy from saved pointers with null fallback, formatted strings render into the payload with bounded size using a copied variable-argument list, masks and socket addresses copy caller bytes with sizes from bit counts or explicit lengths."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__print_flags_u64.alt_1","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__print_symbolic_u64.alt_1","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__print_flags_u64.alt_2","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__print_symbolic_u64.alt_2"],"text":"64-bit flag and symbolic printers have two behaviors: a full path using dedicated 64-bit tables and printers, and a compatibility path that forwards to the 32-bit helpers. Both accept a value plus delimiter or table list in the same positions."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__event_in_hardirq","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__event_in_softirq","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__event_in_irq","include/trace/stages/stage7_class_define.h::__event_in_hardirq","include/trace/stages/stage7_class_define.h::__event_in_softirq","include/trace/stages/stage7_class_define.h::__event_in_irq"],"text":"Interrupt-context tests exist in two encodings: one examines entry trace flags for hard and soft bits and their union, the other examines common flags with bit value 8 for hard, 16 for soft and 24 for either."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__print_ns_to_secs","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__print_ns_without_secs","include/trace/stages/stage7_class_define.h::__print_ns_to_secs","include/trace/stages/stage7_class_define.h::__print_ns_without_secs"],"text":"Nanosecond decomposition divides by one billion to yield whole seconds and separately yields the sub-second remainder. One stage performs the split with a 64-bit division helper on a widened value; another expresses it as division and modulo by the same billion constant."},{"kind":"state_machine","sids":["include/trace/stages/stage1_struct_define.h::TP_STRUCT__entry","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__dynamic_array","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__entry","include/trace/stages/stage4_event_fields.h::__field","include/trace/stages/stage5_get_offsets.h::__entry","include/trace/stages/stage5_get_offsets.h::__dynamic_array","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__entry","include/trace/stages/stage7_class_define.h::__entry"],"text":"The stages form an ordered expansion pipeline for one event declaration: define entry layout, define offset companion, define output rendering, describe exported field metadata, compute per-instance dynamic sizes and offsets while accumulating total payload size, commit offsets and copy payloads at trace time, then define class-level rendering with alternate context and time forms. Each stage redefines the same macro vocabulary to a stage-appropriate meaning and nulls operations irrelevant to that stage."},{"kind":"hazard","sids":["include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__get_dynamic_array","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__get_dynamic_array_len","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__get_rel_dynamic_array_len","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__print_array","include/trace/stages/stage3_trace_output.h::__print_dynamic_array","include/trace/stages/stage4_event_fields.h::__dynamic_array","include/trace/stages/stage4_event_fields.h::__rel_dynamic_array","include/trace/stages/stage5_get_offsets.h::__dynamic_array","include/trace/stages/stage5_get_offsets.h::__rel_dynamic_array","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__assign_str","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__assign_vstr","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__assign_rel_str"],"text":"Location words impose narrow fixed widths: offset and length share 32 bits as two 16-bit halves so large payloads or far offsets cannot be represented, descriptors fix locator size and alignment at four, string copies assume at least one byte for termination, formatted strings truncate to a fixed maximum, and array printing rejects element widths outside one, two, four or eight at build time."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::TRACE_DEFINE_ENUM","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::TRACE_DEFINE_SIZEOF","include/trace/stages/stage5_get_offsets.h::__field","include/trace/stages/stage5_get_offsets.h::__field_ext","include/trace/stages/stage5_get_offsets.h::__field_struct","include/trace/stages/stage5_get_offsets.h::__field_struct_ext","include/trace/stages/stage5_get_offsets.h::__array","include/trace/stages/stage5_get_offsets.h::__sockaddr","include/trace/stages/stage5_get_offsets.h::__rel_sockaddr","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__field","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__field_struct","include/trace/stages/stage6_event_callback.h::__array"],"text":"Many macros intentionally expand to nothing where they carry no information: enum and size helpers and fixed fields plus static arrays in offset and callback stages, and socket or array placeholders where only sizing matters. Field checks in the size-computation stage only validate non-array usage without emitting code."}],"index_id":"99dbddb713e8d299bd55ae3ea6f9df9103f2fe09352557dba05a5a735dfe6c48","lane":24,"pass":1,"prefix_sha256":"37bcfc05d5456f463a61e31f2b52311d5413cb1ef68d3adef8220d9f60942cdb","prompt_sha256":"6c6461fd9a5de44dc5bc1696137eda8e8c1e8b993c5bdb0814b9c346bd3c7383","schema":"lx.extract.v1","sids_read":["include/trace/stages/stage1_struct_define.h::__bitmask","include/trace/stages/stage1_struct_define.h::__cpumask","include/trace/stages/stage1_struct_define.h::__sockaddr","include/trace/stages/stage1_struct_define.h::__rel_dynamic_array","include/trace/stages/stage1_struct_define.h::__rel_string","include/trace/stages/stage1_struct_define.h::__rel_string_len","include/trace/stages/stage1_struct_define.h::__rel_bitmask","include/trace/stages/stage1_struct_define.h::__rel_cpumask","include/trace/stages/stage1_struct_define.h::__rel_sockaddr","include/trace/stages/stage1_struct_define.h::TP_STRUCT__entry","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::TRACE_DEFINE_ENUM","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::TRACE_DEFINE_SIZEOF","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__field","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__field_ext","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__field_struct","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__field_struct_ext","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__array","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__dynamic_array","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__string","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__string_len","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__vstring","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__bitmask","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__cpumask","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__sockaddr","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__rel_dynamic_array","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__rel_string","include/trace/stages/stage2_data_offsets.h::__rel_string_len","include/trace/stages/s